{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2185-12-31 15:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during this admission. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2185-12-31 15:22:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi. I’ve been having a lot of abdominal swelling and pain. It’s been getting worse over the last few days. I also feel like my face is swollen and I’m a bit short of breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2185-12-31 15:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You were here recently with similar symptoms. We’ll need to check if this is another partial bowel obstruction or something else. We’ve already placed an NG tube—did you place that yourself?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2185-12-31 15:25:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I did. I’ve had them before, so I know how. But there wasn’t much output. I’m worried it’s not helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2185-12-31 15:26:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The X-ray shows your large bowel is dilated, which supports the idea of a partial blockage. But we don’t see signs of a complete obstruction. We’ll keep you on bowel rest and IV fluids for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2185-12-31 15:27:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. But what about the swelling in my face and arms? That’s new. Is it related?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2185-12-31 15:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your history of SVC syndrome and previous clots, we’re concerned about venous congestion. We’re ordering an ultrasound and a chest MRV to check your major veins."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2185-12-31 15:30:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that angioplasty I had. Is it possible the narrowing came back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2185-12-31 15:31:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s possible. The narrowing is chronic, but we need to make sure there’s no new clot causing worsening blockage. We’ll know more after the imaging."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2185-12-31 18:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The ultrasound shows a nonocclusive clot in your right subclavian vein. It’s not completely blocked, but we’ll monitor it closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2185-12-31 18:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Again? But I can’t take heparin because of HIT. What can we do?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2185-12-31 18:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. That’s why we’re using fondaparinux. It’s safe for you and will help prevent the clot from getting worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2185-12-31 18:19:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes me feel better. But I’m still really anxious. Being in the hospital brings back bad memories."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2185-12-31 18:20:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’ve noted your PTSD, especially around medical procedures. We’ll try to minimize your time in radiology and keep you informed every step of the way."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2186-01-01 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your C. diff test came back negative, so we don’t think this is an infection. We’re continuing the antibiotics you were on—cipro and flagyl—for your Crohn’s."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2186-01-01 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on Pentasa too. Should I keep taking that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2186-01-01 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re actually holding Pentasa for now. It might be contributing to your low white blood cell count and possibly the swelling. We’ll see how you do without it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2186-01-01 09:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t know it could do that. Okay, I’ll stop it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2186-01-02 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The chest CT shows your SVC is still very narrow—only about 2-3 mm—but there’s flow through it. No new clots. The collateral vessels are doing their job."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2186-01-02 11:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the swelling isn’t from a new blockage?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2186-01-02 11:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not from a new clot, no. But the chronic narrowing could still be causing fluid to back up into your face and arms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2186-01-02 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is there anything we can do about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2186-01-02 11:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re checking your cortisol and C1 esterase levels to rule out other causes. If it’s just from the SVC narrowing, managing the swelling may be about controlling symptoms and monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2186-01-03 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The NG tube needs to be advanced. The X-ray shows it’s sitting in your esophagus. We’ll reposition it to make sure it’s in your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2186-01-03 07:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s uncomfortable. Can’t I just go without it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2186-01-03 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know it’s uncomfortable, but it helps decompress your bowel. Without it, the distention could get worse. We’ll keep it in until your bowels start moving better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2186-01-03 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The MRI shows no active Crohn’s flare and no small bowel obstruction. Your pain seems to come and go, especially during stress or procedures."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2186-01-03 13:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I think the anxiety makes it worse. When I have to go for scans, I get tense and the pain flares."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2186-01-03 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s very common. We’ll keep using diazepam as needed and continue your citalopram. We’re also working with GI to adjust your pain plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2186-01-03 18:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—the X-ray shows improvement in your bowel distention. Your bowels are starting to move again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2186-01-03 18:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Can I start eating soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2186-01-03 18:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start with small sips of water tomorrow and slowly advance your diet if you tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2186-01-04 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood cultures are negative—no infection. We’re continuing the antibiotics as a precaution for Crohn’s."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2186-01-04 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the swelling? Any change?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2186-01-04 10:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still present, but stable. We’re waiting on one more test to rule out a rare cause. For now, we’re focusing on managing symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2186-01-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The ultrasound today shows no DVT in either arm now. The right subclavian clot appears stable or possibly improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2186-01-05 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. But my left arm started hurting last night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2186-01-05 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll get an ultrasound of your left arm right away to check for a new clot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2186-01-06 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The ultrasound shows a new DVT in the superficial brachial vein of your left arm. We’re starting fondaparinux again to treat it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2186-01-06 11:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Another clot? Why is this happening?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2186-01-06 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your history of multiple clots, SVC narrowing, and Crohn’s all increase your risk. We’ll follow up with hematology and vascular surgery to determine how long you need to stay on anticoagulation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2186-01-06 11:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ll do whatever I need to."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2186-01-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat C. diff test is negative. We’re confident there’s no infection driving this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2186-01-07 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my Crohn’s? Is it flaring?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2186-01-07 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The MRI didn’t show active inflammation. We think the symptoms are more from motility issues and partial obstruction, possibly worsened by anxiety."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2186-01-08 10:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The MRV confirms stable findings—chronic narrowing of the SVC and occluded subclavian veins. No new clots. The collateral flow is still working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2186-01-08 10:46:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the swelling might just be chronic?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2186-01-08 10:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’re still waiting on the C1 esterase test to rule out a rare immune cause. But for now, we’ll manage it as chronic venous congestion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2186-01-09 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The ultrasound confirms a completely occlusive DVT in your left brachial vein. We’re continuing fondaparinux as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2186-01-09 16:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need to be on blood thinners for a long time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2186-01-09 16:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely yes. Given your history, hematology will help decide the duration. This new clot reinforces the need for ongoing treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2186-01-10 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing much better. Bowels are moving regularly, pain is down, and you’re tolerating a soft diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2186-01-10 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2186-01-10 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge in the next two days. We’ll make sure your pain and swelling are stable and give you clear instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2186-01-11 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are stable. White count is still low, but we think it’s from the Pentasa, which we’ve stopped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2186-01-11 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the C1 esterase test?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2186-01-11 10:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still pending. You’ll need to follow up with your doctor to get the results and see if further evaluation is needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2186-01-12 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home today. We’re sending you home with fondaparinux, a taper for Dilaudid, and instructions to continue cipro and flagyl."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2186-01-12 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I should stop Pentasa completely?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2186-01-12 09:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Also start omeprazole to protect your stomach. And take diazepam only if your anxiety is severe, for up to two nights."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2186-01-12 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll follow up with hematology and vascular surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2186-01-12 09:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. They’ll guide how long you stay on the blood thinner. Call us if swelling, pain, or shortness of breath worsens."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2186-01-12 09:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better and more in control now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2186-01-12 09:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2185-12-31 15:21:00",
    "admission_end": "2186-01-12 14:43:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 54-year-old woman with a complex history of Crohn’s disease, short bowel syndrome, multiple prior surgeries, and chronic venous thrombosis was admitted for abdominal distention, pain, and facial swelling. Imaging revealed no acute obstruction or Crohn’s flare, but showed chronic SVC narrowing and a nonocclusive right subclavian clot. She developed a new left brachial vein DVT during admission, prompting initiation of fondaparinux, which she continued on discharge. Her symptoms were partially exacerbated by anxiety and PTSD, particularly during procedures. Pentasa was discontinued due to suspected contribution to leukopenia and swelling. She improved with bowel rest, antibiotics, and symptom management, and was discharged home with a pain taper, ongoing anticoagulation, and follow-up plans with hematology and vascular surgery.",
    "problems": [
      "Regional enteritis of unspecified site",
      "Other specified intestinal obstruction",
      "Acute venous embolism and thrombosis of deep veins of upper extremity",
      "Chronic venous embolism and thrombosis of other thoracic veins",
      "Chronic venous embolism and thrombosis of subclavian veins",
      "Posttraumatic stress disorder",
      "Leukocytopenia, unspecified",
      "Other specified agents primarily affecting the gastro-intestinal system causing adverse effects in therapeutic use",
      "Swelling, mass, or lump in head and neck"
    ]
  }
}
